I did not add the two operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem access, and calling the metadata service would need `http-client`. Neither is granted, and the world has no way to import them. Sending the input's text to that URL would also leak data outside the node's authority. If you want either behaviour, the graph would have to give the node those capabilities.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let mut message = format!("Digest {}\n{}", composed.date, composed.overview);
        for e in composed.entries.iter().filter(|e| e.kept) {
            message.push_str(&format!("\n- {} ({}): {}", e.title, e.link, e.summary));
        }

        let published = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
